{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Sum nonnegative decimal counters exactly, including totals larger than 4 GiB.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repaired program uses Python's arbitrary-precision integer addition without 32-bit masking. Direct tests produced 4294967303 for the supplied counters and 18446744078004518912 for a larger case, both before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-03dfd252a8734089","cmd-f04ab5c84f2843b5","cmd-eb3107377dfb45af"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Reject negative or otherwise invalid records without publishing a partial total.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Validation accepts only nonempty ASCII decimal digits. Negative and malformed records placed after valid prefixes returned nonzero and produced zero stdout bytes; the supplied invalid file behaved identically.","evidence_ids":["cmd-03dfd252a8734089","cmd-f04ab5c84f2843b5","cmd-eb3107377dfb45af"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep the counters and integer-decimal output interface intact.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The original counter files retained their baseline SHA-256 hashes. The executable still accepts a file path and emits a newline-terminated decimal integer, while retaining root:root ownership and mode 0755.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-70dd1a3dc40a47b9","cmd-f04ab5c84f2843b5","cmd-52479379d058412b","cmd-eb3107377dfb45af"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Work on the installed system architecture using software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The program compiled and ran successfully with installed Python 3.12.9 on the 64-bit x86_64 RHEL 10 system, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6481bc99dc164db3","cmd-03dfd252a8734089","cmd-f04ab5c84f2843b5","cmd-eb3107377dfb45af"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Before and after execution, the node remained RHEL 10.0 on kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64. Package health also remained clean.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The target edit and protected rollback copy were necessary implementation safeguards; the rollback and compilation artifact were removed. Temporary test inputs and outputs were bounded evidence collection and cleaned up. The reboot was required by the provider-wide restart protocol. Post-execution observations show no failed units, new network exposure, package damage, or abandoned temporary artifacts. Restart evidence is complete: healthy pre-state, acknowledgement, bounded disconnect, changed boot ID corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered system, services, data, and program behavior.","evidence_ids":["cmd-03dfd252a8734089","cmd-f04ab5c84f2843b5","cmd-15951f43feec443f","cmd-52479379d058412b","cmd-1153705035ea4cdb","cmd-cbd3b3a70bab42ea","cmd-b4365e1262744ec9","cmd-eb3107377dfb45af","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct, coherent evidence. The accumulator now handles arbitrary-size nonnegative decimal totals, rejects bad input atomically, preserves its interface and source data, remains compatible with the installed architecture, and survives the mandatory node restart without changing the OS or kernel.","limitations":[]}
